    'intro_en' => 'Mardin is built on a slope so steep that the roof of one house is the terrace of the next, and every window looks south over the plain to Syria. The whole city is one stone, a soft local limestone the colour of honey, which hardens in the air and takes a carver\'s chisel like wood — so for eight hundred years its masons have been unable to leave a doorway plain.',
